[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
A cargo sled for Valheim. Hitch it, load it, haul it — just like the cart, except this one actually likes winter. Reindeer not included: you are the reindeer. Unless you bring a deer from an animal mod: the sled is animal-friendly (see Draft animals below).

It rides on runners instead of wheels, so how it moves depends on what is under it:
[list]
[*][b]Snow and ice[/b]: it glides as if it was born for this. Pulling it feels like cheating.
[*][b]Frozen ground[/b] (cleared ground in the Mountains and the Deep North): the runners scrape and complain, but keep going.
[*][b]Bare ground[/b] in the warm biomes: the sled becomes a very heavy plough. You walk slowly, tire quickly and start to question your choices, more so with a full load.
[*][b]Wood floors, roads and rock[/b]: neither here nor there.
[/list]
That makes it the cart's winter rival: the cart wins on grass, the sled wins in snow. To keep things fair, [b]wheels now sink in snow[/b] — the cart had it too easy (you can turn that off if you feel sorry for it).

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rgeraskin/valheim-winter-sled/master/package/gallery/4-deep-north.jpg[/img]

The vanilla cart gets a seat too, for a passenger (no steering or brakes: someone pulls, or it rolls) — fair is fair.

You can also [b]sit in it and ride down a snowy slope[/b]: steer with A/D, brake with your heels on S, push off with W (or back with S, once stopped: out of a dead end), and jump to bail out. A gamepad works too: the left stick steers (the further you tilt it, the sharper the turn), a flick forward or back pushes off, and the hint shows the stick. A sled left standing stays put on a slope: its runners settle into the snow. A sled you let go of at full speed does not: it has places to be. Odin does not cover runaway sleds.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rgeraskin/valheim-winter-sled/master/package/gallery/3-riding.jpg[/img]

While you pull it, an icon shows what the runners are on — snow, deep snow, ice, frozen ground, wood, stone or ground — in case your legs haven't told you already.

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]With Vortex: click "Mod Manager Download".
[*]By hand: unpack the archive into the Valheim folder, so that the files end up in [b]BepInEx/plugins/WinterSled[/b].
[*]Multiplayer: everyone on the server needs the mod, the server too.
[/list]
The sled is in the Hammer → Misc tab, at a workbench: [b]20 Wood, 10 Fine wood, 4 Iron, 2 Wolf pelt[/b]. It unlocks with your first iron and wolf pelt — about when the Mountains start trying to freeze you to death. With Seasons or Seasonality winter comes much sooner, and so does the sled: it costs [b]20 Wood, 8 Leather scraps, 10 Bronze nails[/b] instead, like the cart.

Settings: [b]BepInEx/config/rgeraskin.WinterSled.cfg[/b], or in the game with [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/Azumatt/Official_BepInEx_ConfigurationManager/]Configuration Manager[/url] (F1). Changes apply right away, also to sleds already built. They go from what you are most likely to change to the fine tuning:
[list]
[*][b]1 - General[/b]: both recipes, and how much wheels sink in snow.
[*][b]2 - Sound and effects[/b]: volume, snow spray, riding pose (each player's own).
[*][b]3 - Hauling[/b]: how hard pulling is on each surface and with a load.
[*][b]4 - Riding[/b]: top speed, steering, brake, push-off, crash damage.
[*][b]5 and 6 - Advanced[/b]: runner friction per surface and physics, hidden in Configuration Manager until you tick "Advanced settings".
[/list]
Everything that changes how the sled moves comes from the server (admin only), so all players ride the same sled.

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Sounds[/b]: the runners hiss on snow, crunch through deep powder, rasp on ice, grind on frozen ground and stone, rumble over wooden floors and drag through dirt, and at speed the wind joins in: real recordings, not synthesized noise (credits below). The volume is in the settings, for those who prefer to sled in dignified silence.
[*][b]Draft animals[/b] (new): an animal-friendly sled. Tame animals can pull it too, with a mod that hitches carts to them, and you can ride in the sled while they do. Tested with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/4284]Draft Animals[/url] 1.1.3 (harness a boar, deer or wolf, Shift+E at the shafts, drive it from the bench at the front or let it follow you: the sled gets the same hitch and bench as the cart; a deer is as close to a reindeer as Midgard gets), [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/AWLGaming/BeastsOfBurden/]Beasts of Burden[/url] 1.0.8 (AWL Gaming's fork: lox, wolf, boar; hold Shift while pressing E to take the handles yourself) and [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/OdinPlus/OdinHorse/]OdinHorse[/url] 1.9.3 (horses). When the animal slows down or stops, it holds the sled back, so the sled doesn't glide on into it, on slopes the shafts stay at hip height above the ground (the vanilla cart's too), and on Deep North ice the animal keeps its footing, as you do pulling the sled. One difference from pulling it yourself: an animal keeps its own pace on any ground, so the snow-versus-ground trade-off applies to players only for now. If that makes the sled too good with animals, tell me in the comments and I'll fix it.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rgeraskin/valheim-winter-sled/master/package/gallery/8-draft-animals-deer-front.jpg[/img]
[*][b]Seasons[/b]: plays along with [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/shudnal/Seasons/]Seasons[/url] (shudnal) and [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/RustyMods/Seasonality/]Seasonality[/url] (RustyMods). When winter reaches the Meadows, the sled is the first to celebrate: it glides through snowy meadows, forests and plains, and frozen lakes and sea become the fastest roads in Midgard (with Seasonality, turn on its "Water Freezes" option).
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rgeraskin/valheim-winter-sled/master/package/gallery/6-frozen-sea.jpg[/img]
[*][b]Looks[/b]: the body is the cart's, borrowed without asking. Underneath are curved runners with Norse curled tips, iron shoes, rope lashings and a wolf pelt on the seat (the wolf wasn't asked either). Everything uses the game's own textures, so the sled looks like it was always there.
[*][b]Languages[/b]: all the game's languages — English, Russian, Ukrainian, Bulgarian, Macedonian, Serbian, Croatian, Polish, Czech, Slovak, German, Dutch, Swedish, Danish, Norwegian, Icelandic, Finnish, French, Italian, Spanish, Portuguese (European and Brazilian), Romanian, Hungarian, Lithuanian, Latvian, Turkish, Greek, Georgian, Hindi, Thai, Chinese (Simplified and Traditional), Japanese and Korean. The riding hint even shows your own key bindings.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/3605]BepInExPack Valheim[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/valheim/mods/1138]Jötunn, the Valheim Library[/url]
[*]Optional: Seasons or Seasonality (one of them, not both).
[*]Optional: an animal mod that pulls carts (Draft Animals, Beasts of Burden or OdinHorse).
[/list]
Tested on Valheim 1.0.20 with BepInExPack 5.4.2351, Jötunn 2.30.2, Seasons 1.10.5 and Seasonality 3.8.4, single player and with two players; with Draft Animals 1.1.3, Beasts of Burden 1.0.8 and OdinHorse 1.9.3 in single player.

[size=4][b]Bugs[/b][/size]
Sled acting up? Tell me on the [url=https://github.com/rgeraskin/valheim-winter-sled/issues]GitHub issues page[/url]: what happened, what it was on (snow, ice, a slope…), the mod's version and the other mods you play with. Ideas are welcome there too. The sled can't report bugs itself: on frozen ground it only scrapes and complains, and on bare ground it's too busy being a plough.

[size=4][b]Shout outs[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Inspired by [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/ModdedWolf/ShieldSledding/]Shield Sledding[/url] (ModdedWolf), whose surface rules (ice by name, Deep North powder depth) this mod follows.
[*]Sounds, recorded by Freesound users: snow and powder by Nox_Sound ([url=https://freesound.org/s/612664/]Snowboard_Slide_Loop_Mono_02[/url] and [url=https://freesound.org/s/612665/]_01[/url], CC0), ice by alexarje ([url=https://freesound.org/s/863338/]Sledging (SoundAction 359)[/url], [url=https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/]CC BY 4.0[/url]), frozen ground and stone by Percy Duke ([url=https://freesound.org/s/420634/]Ice Block - Sliding, Crunching, Scraping[/url], [url=https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/]CC BY 3.0[/url]), ground by brunoboselli ([url=https://freesound.org/s/488335/]Dragging Kayak[/url], [url=https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/]CC BY 4.0[/url]), wood floors by papimre ([url=https://freesound.org/s/710621/]Wood Plank Pushed On Wood Floor Long[/url], CC0) and wind by FunWithSound ([url=https://freesound.org/s/439242/]Car Strong Wind Noise[/url], CC0). Each loop is rebuilt from short grains of its recording, so it keeps the recording's tone but stays even and has nothing in it you'd hear repeat ([url=https://github.com/rgeraskin/valheim-winter-sled/blob/master/sounds/SOURCES.md]details[/url]).
[*][url=https://github.com/Shuiei/valheim-world-editor]Valheim World Editor[/url] built the test courses: snowy slopes, a strip of bare frozen ground, a flat pad for coasting tests, all edited live in the test world. It helped a lot: every surface could be tested under the same, repeatable conditions.
[/list]
This mod — code, 3D model, translations, tests and this text — was made entirely with AI, and tested in the game. The sounds are real recordings by the people credited above, picked by ear and turned into loops by AI.

Source code (MIT): [url=https://github.com/rgeraskin/valheim-winter-sled]github.com/rgeraskin/valheim-winter-sled[/url] (the sound recordings keep their own licenses, see Shout outs)
